# Layout

Single crate `convx`. Not a Cargo workspace. Do not create empty files ahead of the Issue that needs them.

`docs/conventions.md` is created when modules exist. Until then, this file is the layout rule. The public surface lives in `docs/design.ja.md` and `docs/design.md`. Both carry the full specification. The Japanese file is canonical when they differ. Do not copy either into this rule. Do not replace `docs/design.md` with a pointer to the Japanese file.

`docs/roadmap.md` lists work to do: ID, title, Issue, and status. `docs/verification.md` is how a result is checked. Do not write that procedure into the design or the roadmap.

Name the flows that can exist before writing the operation of a flow. A fixture set is not complete before the phase that produces the result. The operation is the judgment and the criteria inside a flow that already has a name.

```text
BAD:  a roadmap section that specifies seeds, generators, and golden commits
GOOD: a roadmap row "Deterministic hull simulations and frozen fixtures"
      and the procedure in docs/verification.md

BAD:  "just gen-fixtures rewrites the files" before any flow exists
GOOD: name the flow (add, extend, revise, retire), then the judgment inside it
```

Do not add a dependency the design does not name. A new dependency is a design change first (`.cursor/rules/workflow.mdc`).

Combinations that would be ignored or rejected at runtime must not be representable (`.cursor/rules/types.mdc`).
